0..78 Comment "// Lazy records: a block of entries `&{.l => e}` answering each label\'s entry,"
79..108 Comment "// and its lazy product type."
109..111 Comment "//"
112..189 Comment "// A lazy record is a lazy product whose entries carry labels, so an entry is"
190..265 Comment "// observed by its label or by its position. A position past the last entry"
266..283 Comment "// names nothing."
284..286 Comment "//"
287..362 Comment "// Each `runs` row observes one entry. A lazy product standing unthunked is"
363..434 Comment "// refused `OutOfFragment.WrongSort`, as is a session type at an entry."
435..437 Comment "//"
438..476 Comment "// - see: #1104 — `spread`, `beyond`"
